---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Values">
  <section class="values-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>What drives the work —</p>
      <h1 class="values-motto" data-reveal>Consumption <span class="motto-symbol">&#8733;</span> Creativity</h1>
      <p class="values-intro" data-reveal>
        Replace this paragraph with your own words — but the idea: what you take in
        directly shapes what you're able to put out. Anime, film, games, music, the
        internet at large — deliberate consumption is the raw material creative work
        gets built from. Cut off the input and the output runs dry.
      </p>

      <div class="values-grid">
        <div class="values-item" data-reveal>
          <h2>Change</h2>
          <p>
            Replace with your own take — e.g. growth through iteration: every project
            is a chance to try a new technique, break an old habit, or push past what
            worked last time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="values-item" data-reveal>
          <h2>Unity</h2>
          <p>
            Replace with your own take — e.g. bringing disparate references (anime,
            live-action, 3D, sound) into one cohesive frame instead of treating them
            as separate disciplines.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="values-item" data-reveal>
          <h2>Equity</h2>
          <p>
            Replace with your own take — e.g. judging work on its craft, not its
            budget or platform: a personal edit gets the same care as a client
            project.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
